WEBVTT

00:00:20.670 --> 00:00:24.220
And that completes my final report until we reach touchdown.

00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:27.800
We're now on full automatic in the hands of the computers.

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:30.000
I've tucked my crew in for the...

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:38.460
long sleep and i'll be joining them soon in less than an hour we'll finish our sixth month out of

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:47.720
cape kennedy six months in deep space by our time that is according to dr hasline's theory of time

00:00:47.720 --> 00:00:53.980
in a vehicle traveling nearly the speed of light the earth has aged nearly 700 years since we left

00:00:53.980 --> 00:00:57.520
it well we've aged hardly at all

00:01:00.990 --> 00:01:07.910
maybe so this much is probably true the men who sent us on this journey are long since dead and

00:01:07.910 --> 00:01:17.120
gone you who are reading me now are different breed i hope a better one i leave the 20th

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:24.500
century with no regrets but one more thing if anybody's listening that is nothing scientific

00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:30.000
it's purely personal seen from out here

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:33.140
Everything seems different.

00:01:34.150 --> 00:01:34.910
Time bends.

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:38.520
Space is boundless.

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:40.920
It squashes a man's ego.

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:44.600
I feel lonely.

00:01:53.870 --> 00:01:54.590
That's about it.

00:01:56.640 --> 00:01:58.680
Tell me, though.

00:02:00.830 --> 00:02:06.860
Does man, that marvel to the universe, that glorious paradox who sent me to the stars,

00:02:07.410 --> 00:02:14.080
still make war against his brother, keep his neighbor's children starving?

00:04:31.790 --> 00:04:32.370
Thank you.

00:07:25.050 --> 00:07:25.670
Stuart?

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:30.610
Stuart.

00:08:31.370 --> 00:08:31.830
Thank you.

00:09:00.760 --> 00:09:14.400
- That's okay, blow the hat before we lose all the power.

00:09:14.400 --> 00:09:18.560
The power's gone, forget it, abandon ship.

00:11:24.120 --> 00:11:26.400
Okay, we're here to stay.

00:11:40.490 --> 00:11:42.450
- Well, where are we?

00:11:42.450 --> 00:11:45.130
Do you have any notions, Skipper?

00:11:45.130 --> 00:11:47.710
- We're some 320 light years from Earth

00:11:47.710 --> 00:11:50.770
on an unnamed planet in orbit around a star

00:11:50.770 --> 00:11:52.870
in the constellation of Orion.

00:11:52.870 --> 00:11:56.910
Is that close enough for you?

00:11:56.910 --> 00:11:59.310
- It could be Bellatrix.

00:11:59.310 --> 00:12:00.000
- It's too right.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:07.950
bellatrix you didn't have time to read the tapes so you really don't know do you what went wrong

00:12:07.950 --> 00:12:14.870
we weren't programmed to land in the water the question is not so much where we are as when we

00:12:14.870 --> 00:12:21.360
are all right we've had enough sleep to hold us for a while let's start earning all that back pay

00:13:00.510 --> 00:13:05.210
- Dodge, run your soil test.

00:13:05.210 --> 00:13:07.360
Got your sensors?

00:13:07.360 --> 00:13:08.120
- Right.

00:13:08.120 --> 00:13:09.200
- Geiger cutter?

00:13:09.200 --> 00:13:13.060
- Got it.

00:13:13.060 --> 00:13:16.870
- Let's see, one pistol, 20 rounds ammo,

00:13:16.870 --> 00:13:20.470
a medical kit, camera, TX-9.

00:13:20.470 --> 00:13:25.060
We've got food and water enough for three days.

00:13:25.060 --> 00:13:27.340
- How long is a day?

00:13:27.340 --> 00:13:28.780
- That's a good question.

00:13:28.780 --> 00:13:29.510
Landon.

00:13:30.600 --> 00:13:34.390
Hey, Landon! Join the expedition.

00:13:34.390 --> 00:13:41.490
Sorry, I was thinking about Stuart. What do you suppose happened?

00:13:41.490 --> 00:13:43.800
Hair leak. She died in her sleep.

00:13:43.800 --> 00:13:46.100
You don't seem very cut up about it.

00:13:46.100 --> 00:13:50.600
It's a little late for her wake. She's been dead nearly a year.

00:13:50.600 --> 00:13:53.740
That means we've been away from Earth for 18 months.

00:13:53.740 --> 00:13:57.910
Aren't I? You've gone gray.

00:14:00.380 --> 00:14:04.780
Apart from that, you look pretty chipper for a man who's 2,031 years old.

00:14:04.780 --> 00:14:08.930
I read the clocks. They bare out Hasslein's hypothesis.

00:14:08.930 --> 00:14:13.960
We have been away from Earth for 2,000 years, give or take a decade.

00:14:13.960 --> 00:14:18.110
Still can't accept it.

00:14:18.110 --> 00:14:22.560
Time's wiped out everything you ever knew. It's all dust.

00:14:22.560 --> 00:14:28.310
Prove it. If we can't get back, it's still just a theory.

00:14:28.310 --> 00:14:29.830
It's a fact, Landon.

00:14:30.090 --> 00:14:32.260
Buy it. You'll sleep better.

00:14:32.260 --> 00:14:37.350
Nothing will grow here. There's just a trace of carbohydrates.

00:14:37.350 --> 00:14:39.830
All the nitrogen is locked into the nitrates.

00:14:39.830 --> 00:14:43.160
- No dangerous ionization? - No.

00:14:43.160 --> 00:14:50.180
Well, if there's no life here, we've got just 72 hours to find it.

00:14:50.180 --> 00:14:53.670
That's when the groceries run out. Let's go.

00:14:53.670 --> 00:14:58.630
- Which direction? - That way.

00:14:58.630 --> 00:15:00.000
Any particular reason?

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:07.090
- No reason? - None at all.

00:15:07.090 --> 00:15:14.890
Come on.

00:18:01.790 --> 00:18:02.630
- Order check.

00:18:20.070 --> 00:18:22.310
- It doesn't add up.

00:18:22.310 --> 00:18:24.460
Thunder and lightning and no rain.

00:18:24.460 --> 00:18:28.270
Cloud cover at night, that strange luminosity,

00:18:28.270 --> 00:18:30.000
yet there's no moon.

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:36.450
fix what would that tell you i've told you where you are and when you are all right all right

00:18:36.450 --> 00:18:44.890
you're 300 light years from your precious planet your loved ones are dead and forgotten for 20

00:18:44.890 --> 00:18:49.790
centuries 20 centuries even if you could get back they'd think you were something that fell

00:18:49.790 --> 00:18:55.440
out of a tree i'd tell her quit writing him there is just one reality left we are here

00:18:55.440 --> 00:18:58.480
and it is now you get hold of that and hang on to it you might as well be dead

00:19:00.060 --> 00:19:09.560
to die he's prepared to die ha doesn't that make you misty chalk up another

00:19:09.560 --> 00:19:22.660
victory for the human spirit clue me in on something will you why did you sign

00:19:22.660 --> 00:19:30.000
on for this trip you volunteer why never mind I'll clue you in you were the golden

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:32.200
boy of the class of '72.

00:19:32.200 --> 00:19:33.800
When they nominated you for the big one,

00:19:33.800 --> 00:19:35.200
you couldn't turn it down.

00:19:35.200 --> 00:19:38.450
Not without losing your all-American image.

00:19:38.450 --> 00:19:40.280
Climb off, will you?

00:19:40.280 --> 00:19:41.480
Oh, and the glory.

00:19:41.480 --> 00:19:43.530
Don't forget that.

00:19:43.530 --> 00:19:46.330
There's a life-size bronze statue of you

00:19:46.330 --> 00:19:48.400
standing out there somewhere.

00:19:48.400 --> 00:19:50.100
Well, it's probably turned green by now.

00:19:50.100 --> 00:19:52.230
Nobody can read the name plate.

00:19:52.230 --> 00:19:54.530
But never let it be said that we forget our heroes.

00:19:54.530 --> 00:19:56.930
Tell her, I'm telling you to climb off my back.

00:19:56.930 --> 00:20:00.000
And there's one last item, immortality.

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:03.800
- You wanted to live forever, didn't you? - Well, you damn near made it.

00:20:03.800 --> 00:20:08.340
Except for me and Dodge, you've lived longer than anyone ever born.

00:20:08.340 --> 00:20:15.850
And with our lovely Lieutenant Stewart dead, it looks like you're the last of the line.

00:20:15.850 --> 00:20:20.150
You got what you wanted, Tiger. How does it taste?

00:20:20.150 --> 00:20:25.960
Okay, you read me well enough. But why can't I read you?

00:20:25.960 --> 00:20:30.000
- Don't bother. - Dodge there, he's not like me at all.

00:20:30.860 --> 00:20:34.010
- But he makes sense.

00:20:34.010 --> 00:20:36.190
He'd walk naked into a live volcano

00:20:36.190 --> 00:20:37.490
if he thought he could learn something

00:20:37.490 --> 00:20:39.980
that no other man knew.

00:20:39.980 --> 00:20:43.670
But you, you're no seeker.

00:20:43.670 --> 00:20:44.960
You're negative.

00:20:44.960 --> 00:20:47.120
- And I'm not prepared to die.

00:20:47.120 --> 00:20:49.060
- I'd like to know why not.

00:20:49.060 --> 00:20:51.260
You thought life on earth was meaningless.

00:20:51.260 --> 00:20:53.280
You despise people.

00:20:53.280 --> 00:20:54.540
So what'd you do?

00:20:54.540 --> 00:20:55.600
You ran out.

00:20:55.600 --> 00:20:58.860
- No, no, it's not like that, Landon.

00:20:58.860 --> 00:21:00.000
I'm a seeker too.

00:21:01.080 --> 00:21:02.560
But my dreams aren't like yours.

00:21:03.490 --> 00:21:05.670
I can't help thinking somewhere in the universe

00:21:05.670 --> 00:21:07.930
there has to be something better than man.

00:21:08.490 --> 00:21:09.250
Has to be.

00:21:53.740 --> 00:21:54.390
Life.

00:22:09.660 --> 00:22:13.860
For there's one, there's another, and another, and another.

00:22:14.620 --> 00:22:15.550
Let's find him.

00:24:51.500 --> 00:24:55.120
Skipper, look.

00:25:03.800 --> 00:25:16.120
- Scarecrows? - Let's see.

00:26:02.520 --> 00:26:05.090
To hell with the scarecrows.

00:27:30.380 --> 00:27:31.320
Look at this.

00:29:44.650 --> 00:29:46.000
They didn't leave much, did they?

00:30:17.150 --> 00:30:20.590
- Well, at least they haven't tried to bite us.

00:30:20.590 --> 00:30:30.000
- Blessed are the vegetarians.

00:30:30.000 --> 00:30:48.350
human but i think they're mute we got off at the wrong stop you're supposed to be the optimist

00:30:48.350 --> 00:30:54.710
landon look in the bright side this is the best they've got around here in six months we'll be

00:30:54.710 --> 00:30:55.710
running this planet

00:32:30.440 --> 00:32:30.900
Whoa.

00:35:59.500 --> 00:36:00.000
Smile.

00:36:00.860 --> 00:36:04.420
Oh, oh, oh, oh.

00:36:40.810 --> 00:36:45.110
- Which one was wearing the strange clothes? - This one.

00:36:48.150 --> 00:36:51.730
- Will he live? - I don't know.

00:36:52.460 --> 00:36:54.740
This beast has lost a lot of blood.

00:37:01.850 --> 00:37:04.960
- There's no probe here. Find one. - Yes, sir.

00:37:05.240 --> 00:37:08.420
This place is dirty, Doctor.

00:37:08.720 --> 00:37:11.810
Doctor, these animals are dirty.

00:37:12.040 --> 00:37:14.920
They stink and they carry communicable diseases.

00:37:15.120 --> 00:37:17.440
Why aren't they cleaned up before they're brought here?

00:37:17.470 --> 00:37:19.300
You don't sound happy in your work.

00:37:19.650 --> 00:37:22.150
Little more than a vet in this laboratory.

00:37:22.640 --> 00:37:25.510
You promised to speak to Dr. Zaius about me.

00:37:25.780 --> 00:37:29.640
I did. You know how he looks down his nose at chimpanzees.

00:37:30.060 --> 00:37:32.400
The quota system's been abolished.

00:37:32.400 --> 00:37:33.400
You made it?

00:37:33.400 --> 00:37:34.320
Why can't I?

00:37:34.320 --> 00:37:35.380
What do you mean, "made it"?

00:37:35.380 --> 00:37:37.730
I'm an animal psychologist, that's all.

00:37:37.730 --> 00:37:39.990
We have no authority.

00:37:39.990 --> 00:37:43.130
You do all right when it comes to getting space and equipment.

00:37:43.130 --> 00:37:47.520
That's because Dr. Zeiss realizes our work has value.

00:37:47.520 --> 00:37:53.050
The foundations of scientific brain surgery are being laid right here, in studies of cerebral

00:37:53.050 --> 00:37:54.610
functions of these animals.

00:37:54.610 --> 00:38:00.000
They're still dirty, Doctor, and the bite is septic.

00:38:00.000 --> 00:38:04.550
Now, look at that. Hold his jaw.

00:38:30.410 --> 00:38:31.350
Good morning, Dr. Zira.

00:38:31.510 --> 00:38:32.190
Good morning, Julius.

00:38:32.590 --> 00:38:33.710
How's our patient today?

00:38:34.030 --> 00:38:34.730
No change.

00:38:35.110 --> 00:38:37.110
The minute you open the door, he goes into his act.

00:38:40.090 --> 00:38:44.060
Do we want this morning?

00:38:44.470 --> 00:38:45.600
Do we want something?

00:38:46.020 --> 00:38:47.070
Come on, speak.

00:38:48.070 --> 00:38:49.730
Come on, speak.

00:38:50.900 --> 00:38:52.440
Do we want some sugar, old-timer?

00:38:52.720 --> 00:38:57.260
You could get hurt doing that, doctor.

00:38:57.790 --> 00:38:58.690
Oh, don't be silly.

00:38:58.810 --> 00:39:00.000
He's perfectly tamed.

00:39:00.120 --> 00:39:02.580
Ah, they're all tame until they take a chunk out of you.

00:39:03.070 --> 00:39:06.270
Well, Bright Eyes, is our throat feeling better?

00:39:08.190 --> 00:39:09.890
Still hurts, doesn't it?

00:39:10.070 --> 00:39:12.890
See? He keeps pretending he can talk.

00:39:16.270 --> 00:39:18.280
Bright Eyes is remarkable.

00:39:19.330 --> 00:39:21.430
He keeps trying to form words.

00:39:22.130 --> 00:39:24.530
You know what they say, humans see, humans do.

00:39:30.320 --> 00:39:32.010
- Now what?

00:39:32.010 --> 00:39:37.940
- He seems to want something.

00:39:37.940 --> 00:39:40.160
- I'd be careful, Doctor.

00:39:40.160 --> 00:39:41.240
What did I tell you?

00:39:41.240 --> 00:39:45.270
- I'll try it again and I'll break your arm!

00:39:45.270 --> 00:39:49.050
- Good morning, Your Excellency.

00:39:49.050 --> 00:39:52.700
- Dr. Zayas.

00:39:52.700 --> 00:39:55.470
- Good morning, sir.

00:39:55.470 --> 00:39:57.260
- Open up, please.

00:39:57.260 --> 00:39:59.000
- I'm so glad you could come.

00:40:00.510 --> 00:40:01.510
He's over here.

00:40:01.510 --> 00:40:04.860
Bright eyes.

00:40:04.860 --> 00:40:07.350
Show him.

00:40:07.350 --> 00:40:08.650
Go ahead.

00:40:08.650 --> 00:40:09.650
Do your trick.

00:40:09.650 --> 00:40:11.980
Speak.

00:40:11.980 --> 00:40:13.640
Go on.

00:40:13.640 --> 00:40:14.640
Speak again.

00:40:14.640 --> 00:40:18.500
There.

00:40:18.500 --> 00:40:19.830
Can you believe it?

00:40:19.830 --> 00:40:21.580
Yes, amusing.

00:40:21.580 --> 00:40:23.580
A man acting like an ape.

00:40:23.580 --> 00:40:30.000
Josias, I could swear he's a man.

00:40:30.410 --> 00:40:33.590
He has a definite gift for mimicry.

00:40:33.670 --> 00:40:38.970
Most unusual. He's using that old blanket as clothing.

00:40:39.050 --> 00:40:44.360
I wonder how he'd score on a Hopkins Manual dexterity test.

00:40:44.440 --> 00:40:49.720
- An animal? - Look, he's moving his fingers.

00:40:49.800 --> 00:40:52.120
Only because he saw you moving yours.

00:40:52.200 --> 00:40:55.160
No, but perhaps he understood.

00:40:55.240 --> 00:40:58.680
Man has no understanding.

00:41:00.000 --> 00:41:03.000
and be taught a few simple tricks. Nothing more.

00:41:03.010 --> 00:41:07.470
I'm afraid I must disagree. According to my experiments...

00:41:07.570 --> 00:41:10.860
Dr. Zehrer, I must caution you.

00:41:11.660 --> 00:41:15.660
Experimental brain surgery on these creatures is one thing,

00:41:15.760 --> 00:41:17.310
and I'm all in favor of it.

00:41:17.930 --> 00:41:21.030
But your behavioral studies are something else again.

00:41:21.600 --> 00:41:26.740
To suggest that we can learn anything about the simian nature

00:41:26.840 --> 00:41:29.440
from a study of man is sheer nonsense.

00:41:30.480 --> 00:41:32.790
That man is a nuisance.

00:41:32.790 --> 00:41:36.350
He eats up his food supplies in the forest,

00:41:36.350 --> 00:41:43.560
then migrates to our green belts and ravages our crops.

00:41:43.560 --> 00:41:47.860
The sooner he is exterminated, the better.

00:41:47.860 --> 00:41:51.000
It's a question of simian survival.

00:42:02.780 --> 00:42:06.650
Is this the one you wanted, Doctor?

00:42:06.650 --> 00:42:08.700
Ah, yes, thank you.

00:42:08.700 --> 00:42:10.480
Bright eyes.

00:42:10.480 --> 00:42:21.210
I've got a present for you.

00:42:21.210 --> 00:42:24.800
With him!

00:43:19.580 --> 00:43:21.090
Up here.

00:43:21.090 --> 00:43:23.940
Do you have to work tonight?

00:43:23.940 --> 00:43:25.510
No.

00:43:25.510 --> 00:43:26.310
Neither do I.

00:43:31.760 --> 00:43:55.590
- Cornelius, right eyes, what I was telling you about.

00:43:55.590 --> 00:43:56.720
- What's so special about him?

00:44:00.000 --> 00:44:11.760
bright eyes has her throat today she remembers remembers what the blood

00:44:11.760 --> 00:44:17.090
transfusion Sarah really you know they can't hey watch out here comes number

00:44:17.090 --> 00:44:22.590
one something's bothering him he's been trying around the lab for the last two

00:44:22.590 --> 00:44:30.000
days good morning dr. Zayas you know my dr. Cornelius my fiance of course

00:44:30.000 --> 00:44:32.000
The young ape with a shovel.

00:44:32.000 --> 00:44:34.820
I hear you're planning another archaeological expedition.

00:44:34.820 --> 00:44:36.810
With the Academy's approval, sir.

00:44:36.810 --> 00:44:39.810
The project will require my support, of course.

00:44:39.810 --> 00:44:41.810
I hope I may count on it, sir.

00:44:41.810 --> 00:44:43.790
Cornelius, a friendly warning.

00:44:43.790 --> 00:44:49.270
As you dig for artifacts, be sure you don't bury your reputation.

00:45:30.760 --> 00:45:31.660
You've heard him.

00:45:31.920 --> 00:45:34.210
You've heard him inside.

00:45:38.300 --> 00:45:38.820
Cornelius?

00:45:39.970 --> 00:45:42.110
Cornelius, if you have a moment today,

00:45:42.190 --> 00:45:45.590
I'd like to discuss this expedition of yours in more detail.

00:45:46.100 --> 00:45:46.900
Oh, certainly, sir.

00:45:46.920 --> 00:45:48.820
I'll pick up my notes and I'll come right over.

00:45:50.090 --> 00:45:52.370
I don't understand these animal psychologists.

00:45:52.930 --> 00:45:54.910
What's Dr. Zero trying to prove?

00:45:55.660 --> 00:45:58.120
That man can be domesticated.

00:45:58.980 --> 00:46:00.000
Ha, ha, ha, ha!

00:46:00.320 --> 00:46:01.540
Ha, ha, ha, ha.

00:46:37.450 --> 00:46:38.290
- What happened?

00:46:38.290 --> 00:46:40.400
- Oh, those fools and their torches.

00:46:40.400 --> 00:46:41.520
Do you have any ointment?

00:46:41.520 --> 00:46:46.160
- I'll see.

00:46:46.160 --> 00:46:49.940
- Sorry, bright eyes.

00:47:00.760 --> 00:47:02.240
I told you what you'd get!

00:47:02.480 --> 00:47:04.620
Julius, don't, don't, don't! It doesn't matter!

00:47:05.470 --> 00:47:06.690
Julius, don't hurt him!

00:47:18.090 --> 00:47:19.870
Natural-born thieves, aren't they?

00:47:33.640 --> 00:47:35.840
Get me a collar and leash.

00:47:36.660 --> 00:47:38.120
I'm taking him out of here.

00:47:38.240 --> 00:47:39.220
He's vicious, Doctor.

00:47:39.820 --> 00:47:41.360
Besides, it's against the rules.

00:47:41.440 --> 00:47:58.420
Do as I say, Jewel.

00:48:01.400 --> 00:48:20.580
- Taylor? - It's a stunt.

00:48:20.920 --> 00:48:23.110
Ah, humans can't write.

00:48:23.130 --> 00:48:25.380
Dear, you're a scientist.

00:48:25.540 --> 00:48:27.620
Don't you believe your own eyes?

00:48:32.330 --> 00:48:37.920
How did you learn to do this?

00:48:37.920 --> 00:48:54.900
Jefferson Public School, Fort Wayne, Indiana.

00:48:54.900 --> 00:48:57.720
Back on that planet you say you came from?

00:48:57.720 --> 00:48:59.800
Uh-huh.

00:49:04.860 --> 00:49:20.430
maybe he is intelligent he's also crazy cornelius cornelius please dodge was killed in the hunt

00:49:21.280 --> 00:49:30.000
what happened to landon i don't know they fell out of

00:49:30.000 --> 00:49:36.080
of the sky with you.

00:49:36.080 --> 00:49:38.310
- Not fell, flew.

00:49:38.310 --> 00:49:41.020
- Flight is a scientific impossibility.

00:49:41.020 --> 00:49:43.890
- And even if it would, why fly?

00:49:43.890 --> 00:49:45.110
Where would it get you?

00:50:02.970 --> 00:50:04.770
Do you have maps?

00:50:08.180 --> 00:50:22.760
Watch it here.

00:50:22.760 --> 00:50:27.650
You fell into the water here?

00:50:28.280 --> 00:50:30.000
You came ashore.

00:50:30.380 --> 00:50:40.760
...marched across the desert, mountains, many days and nights, and reached the jungle?

00:50:40.760 --> 00:50:43.760
Out of the question.

00:50:43.760 --> 00:50:49.050
Cornelius, why do you insist on provoking him?

00:50:49.050 --> 00:50:54.170
No creature can survive in the Forbidden Zone. I know, I've been there, I've seen it.

00:50:54.170 --> 00:50:59.250
Then how do you account for me?

00:51:00.190 --> 00:51:06.940
- I don't, and I'm not going to try.

00:51:06.940 --> 00:51:10.150
- What about your theory?

00:51:10.150 --> 00:51:13.800
The existence of someone like Taylor might prove it.

00:51:13.800 --> 00:51:15.930
- Vera, do you want to get my head chopped off?

00:51:15.930 --> 00:51:17.510
- Don't be foolish.

00:51:17.510 --> 00:51:20.010
If it's true, they'll have to accept it.

00:51:20.010 --> 00:51:22.980
- Oh, no they won't.

00:51:22.980 --> 00:51:26.520
- Cornelius has developed the most brilliant hypothesis.

00:51:26.520 --> 00:51:28.090
- But I'm probably wrong.

00:51:28.090 --> 00:51:30.000
- That the ape evolved.

00:51:30.000 --> 00:51:33.880
from a lower order of primate, possibly man.

00:51:34.310 --> 00:51:36.790
In his trip to the Forbidden Zone,

00:51:36.930 --> 00:51:41.610
he discovered traces of a culture older than recorded time.

00:51:41.690 --> 00:51:43.600
The evidence was very meager.

00:51:43.720 --> 00:51:45.060
You didn't think so then?

00:51:45.140 --> 00:51:48.790
That was before Dr. Zayas and half of the Academy said that my idea was heresy.

00:51:49.050 --> 00:51:52.030
How can scientific truth be heresy?

00:51:52.600 --> 00:51:55.890
What it tailor is exactly the proof you needed.

00:51:56.060 --> 00:51:59.600
A mutation, a missing link,

00:52:00.000 --> 00:52:03.110
between the unevolved primate and the ape.

00:52:05.880 --> 00:52:08.160
Touchy, isn't he?

00:52:09.280 --> 00:52:11.040
I am not a missing link.

00:52:11.780 --> 00:52:15.360
Well, if you were a missing link, the sacred scrolls wouldn't be worth their parchment.

00:52:16.330 --> 00:52:18.470
Well, maybe they're not.

00:52:20.220 --> 00:52:21.520
Oh, no, thank you.

00:52:21.720 --> 00:52:23.320
I'm not going to get into that battle.

00:52:23.520 --> 00:52:25.020
Cornelia, show some strength.

00:52:25.220 --> 00:52:26.280
Zira, listen to me.

00:52:27.490 --> 00:52:29.280
Now, we both have fine futures.

00:52:30.000 --> 00:52:34.100
a marriage, stimulating careers. I'm up for a raise.

00:52:36.200 --> 00:52:37.170
Dr. Zaius.

00:52:37.170 --> 00:52:41.500
Did you forget our appointment, Cornelius?

00:52:41.500 --> 00:52:43.500
Oh, no, sir. I was just collecting my notes.

00:52:43.500 --> 00:52:48.460
You know Dr. Maximus, of course, our Commissioner for Animal Affairs.

00:52:48.460 --> 00:52:51.980
Yes, sir. It's a pleasure to see you again.

00:52:51.980 --> 00:52:53.220
What is that?

00:52:53.220 --> 00:52:55.220
A man, Dr. Maximus.

00:52:55.220 --> 00:53:00.000
I know it's a man. And you know the rules. No animal.

00:53:00.220 --> 00:53:03.880
allowed outside the compound, and most especially not without a leash.

00:53:03.980 --> 00:53:09.030
Yes, sir, but this creature is a special case.

00:53:09.060 --> 00:53:10.980
Why special?

00:53:11.020 --> 00:53:14.310
We're conducting a new experiment.

00:53:14.340 --> 00:53:17.250
Wouldn't that more properly be done in your office?

00:53:17.350 --> 00:53:19.040
Yes, sir.

00:53:19.420 --> 00:53:22.890
Guards, return this beast to the compound.

00:53:22.920 --> 00:53:25.440
What is this?

00:53:28.430 --> 00:53:29.890
Toy.

00:53:31.630 --> 00:53:32.630
- It's on the air.

00:53:32.630 --> 00:53:33.680
- Zero.

00:53:33.680 --> 00:53:35.710
- Try it.

00:53:35.710 --> 00:53:36.980
- Nonsense.

00:53:36.980 --> 00:53:57.240
- What's up, Lieutenant?

00:53:57.240 --> 00:54:00.000
- We're taking number four over to surgery in five minutes.

00:54:00.000 --> 00:54:05.650
- How come? The beast's throat's nearly healed. - It's not his throat this time. The vet's gonna gild him.

00:54:05.650 --> 00:54:09.090
Dr. Zero won't like it. She wants that pair to mate.

00:54:09.090 --> 00:54:13.250
These orders come from Dr. Zaius himself. There's nothing she can do about it.

00:54:30.030 --> 00:54:34.700
Only you knew what they're going to do.

00:54:34.700 --> 00:54:41.520
Stay still now, don't give me any trouble.

00:55:11.160 --> 00:55:20.080
you must but make an end of sorrow he lives again yes he has found peace

00:55:20.080 --> 00:55:29.440
in heaven he was a model for us all a gorilla to remember hunter

00:55:30.000 --> 00:55:40.780
Warrior, defender of the faith, cherished husband, beloved father, generous master, yes.

00:55:42.660 --> 00:55:45.500
He was a fond of Simeon kindness.

00:55:47.610 --> 00:55:54.220
The dear departed once said to me, I never met an ape I didn't like.

00:55:55.510 --> 00:55:56.930
Look, it's a man.

00:55:56.930 --> 00:56:00.000
In heaven's name, get rid of that creature.

00:56:00.030 --> 00:56:12.040
Touch him! Touch him!

00:56:31.950 --> 00:56:32.400
Come on.

00:59:01.310 --> 00:59:02.980
- I don't want to see it!

01:00:00.000 --> 01:00:17.950
the ministry of science take your stinking paws off me you damn dirty ape listen to me

01:00:31.310 --> 01:00:31.890
You...

01:01:30.060 --> 01:01:33.170
It's a man! A man!

01:01:42.900 --> 01:01:48.230
Now I don't even have you.

01:01:49.270 --> 01:01:52.250
Imagine me needing someone.

01:01:53.260 --> 01:01:54.550
Back on Earth, I never did.

01:01:54.950 --> 01:02:00.000
Oh, there were women, lots of women, lots of lovemaking, but no love.

01:02:01.020 --> 01:02:03.180
That was the kind of world we'd made.

01:02:03.910 --> 01:02:07.750
So I left, because there was no one to hold me there.

01:02:08.310 --> 01:02:10.430
Did I tell you about Stuart?

01:02:10.800 --> 01:02:15.800
There was a lovely girl, the most precious cargo we brought along.

01:02:15.900 --> 01:02:23.710
She was to be the new Eve, with our hot and eager help, of course.

01:02:25.650 --> 01:02:28.350
Probably just as well she didn't make it this far.

01:02:32.490 --> 01:02:35.440
love me, I wonder. Can you

01:02:35.440 --> 01:02:47.670
love? You're not as smart as

01:02:47.670 --> 01:02:50.650
Stuart, but you're the only girl

01:02:50.650 --> 01:02:58.070
in town. Look at that.

01:03:00.440 --> 01:03:01.730
Touched a smile.

01:04:27.420 --> 01:04:30.000
weeks. What happened? Where have you

01:04:30.670 --> 01:04:33.030
- Why didn't you come see me?

01:04:33.030 --> 01:04:33.870
What is this?

01:04:33.870 --> 01:04:34.790
- I'm hearing.

01:04:34.790 --> 01:04:36.150
- Be clever, be quiet.

01:04:36.150 --> 01:04:51.700
- All right!

01:04:51.700 --> 01:04:54.080
- Sad hoc tribunal of the National Academy

01:04:54.080 --> 01:04:55.080
is now in session.

01:04:55.080 --> 01:04:57.790
President of the Academy presiding.

01:04:57.790 --> 01:05:00.000
On my right, Dr. Maximus, commissioner.

01:05:00.000 --> 01:05:03.050
for animal affairs, and on my left, Dr. Zayas,

01:05:03.050 --> 01:05:06.980
Minister of Science and Chief Defender of the Faith,

01:05:06.980 --> 01:05:09.190
and appearing for the state, Dr. Honorius,

01:05:09.190 --> 01:05:11.080
Deputy Minister of Justice.

01:05:11.080 --> 01:05:16.480
Bailiff!

01:05:16.480 --> 01:05:19.560
You had instructions to clean up the beast.

01:05:19.560 --> 01:05:23.230
These rags he's wearing give off a stench

01:05:23.230 --> 01:05:26.230
that's offensive to the dignity of this tribunal.

01:05:37.480 --> 01:05:39.180
You may proceed, Dr. Honora.

01:05:39.940 --> 01:05:41.160
By your leave, Mr. President,

01:05:41.500 --> 01:05:45.520
this tribunal has not yet defined the purpose for this inquiry.

01:05:47.720 --> 01:05:51.280
You ask for the opportunity to present your case.

01:05:51.660 --> 01:05:53.500
Surely you must know why you're here.

01:05:53.660 --> 01:05:56.700
At the very least, this man has the right to know

01:05:56.700 --> 01:05:58.780
whether there's a charge against him.

01:05:59.000 --> 01:05:59.760
Objection!

01:06:00.190 --> 01:06:05.210
This exhibit is indeed a man, therefore he has no rights under eight law.

01:06:05.210 --> 01:06:09.050
Dr. Zira, this is a man, is it not?

01:06:09.050 --> 01:06:15.380
He is unlike any man you have ever seen, as we hope to prove.

01:06:15.380 --> 01:06:18.590
Answer the question, Dr. Zira. Is it a man?

01:06:18.590 --> 01:06:22.560
Sir, perhaps the question is the pointed issue.

01:06:22.560 --> 01:06:27.480
Is he a man, is he deviant, or a freak of nature?

01:06:27.480 --> 01:06:28.480
Objection.

01:06:28.480 --> 01:06:30.000
Sustained.

01:06:30.000 --> 01:06:36.070
Now, Dr. Zehra, in all fairness, you must admit that the accused is a non-ape

01:06:36.170 --> 01:06:38.870
and therefore has no rights under ape law.

01:06:38.890 --> 01:06:41.300
Then why is he called the accused?

01:06:41.550 --> 01:06:44.250
Your honors must think him guilty of something.

01:06:46.900 --> 01:06:50.760
It is not being tried. It's being disposed of.

01:06:51.210 --> 01:06:55.300
It is scientific heresy that is being tried here.

01:06:55.400 --> 01:06:57.200
Well put, Dr. Zehra.

01:06:57.840 --> 01:07:00.000
Let us warn our friends that they are needed.

01:07:00.000 --> 01:07:04.180
to endanger their own careers by defending this animal.

01:07:05.300 --> 01:07:07.400
Then I'll defend myself.

01:07:07.400 --> 01:07:16.200
Dr. Zero, would you tell Bright Eyes to be quiet?

01:07:16.260 --> 01:07:19.240
- My name is Taylor. - Silence the animal!

01:07:20.170 --> 01:07:22.660
Wait, let me...

01:07:24.440 --> 01:07:27.080
You may proceed, Mr. Prosecutor.

01:07:27.480 --> 01:07:30.000
No any judges. My case is...

01:07:30.000 --> 01:07:32.590
based on our first article of faith,

01:07:32.590 --> 01:07:35.960
that the Almighty created the ape in his own image,

01:07:35.960 --> 01:07:37.950
that he gave him a soul and a mind,

01:07:37.950 --> 01:07:41.320
that he set him apart from the beasts of the jungle

01:07:41.320 --> 01:07:43.150
and made him the lord of the planet.

01:07:43.150 --> 01:07:46.930
These sacred truths are self-evident.

01:07:46.930 --> 01:07:50.850
The proper study of apes is apes.

01:07:50.850 --> 01:07:55.500
But certain young cynics have chosen to study man.

01:07:55.500 --> 01:07:59.730
Yes, perverted scientists.

01:08:00.000 --> 01:08:02.080
advance an insidious theory called

01:08:02.080 --> 01:08:03.080
evolution.

01:08:03.480 --> 01:08:06.060
Come to the point, Dr. Lenorez.

01:08:06.570 --> 01:08:07.930
The state charges that

01:08:07.930 --> 01:08:10.130
Dr. Zira and a corrupt surgeon

01:08:10.130 --> 01:08:12.110
named Galen experimented

01:08:12.110 --> 01:08:13.170
on this wounded animal,

01:08:13.780 --> 01:08:15.840
tampering with his brain and throat tissues

01:08:15.840 --> 01:08:18.610
to produce a speaking monster.

01:08:18.900 --> 01:08:19.980
That's a lie!

01:08:20.140 --> 01:08:21.480
Mind your tongue, madam.

01:08:21.900 --> 01:08:24.540
Did we create his mind as well?

01:08:25.290 --> 01:08:26.830
Not only can this man speak,

01:08:27.260 --> 01:08:28.220
he can think,

01:08:28.220 --> 01:08:30.000
he can reason.

01:08:33.130 --> 01:08:40.720
reason with the tribunal's permission allow me to expose this hoax by direct examination proceed

01:08:40.720 --> 01:08:53.730
doctor but do not turn this hearing into a farce tell the court bright eyes what is the second

01:08:53.730 --> 01:09:00.000
article of faith i know nothing of your culture i i admit that of course

01:09:00.000 --> 01:09:02.880
he doesn't know our culture because he cannot think.

01:09:02.950 --> 01:09:08.390
Tell us, why are all apes created equal?

01:09:08.470 --> 01:09:12.560
Some apes, it seems, are more equal than others.

01:09:12.640 --> 01:09:17.670
Ridiculous. Tell us, bright eyes, why do men have no souls?

01:09:17.670 --> 01:09:22.940
What is the proof that a divine spark exists in the simian brain?

01:09:32.750 --> 01:09:50.310
this for me. Since the defendant has been forbidden to speak in his own defense, he requests that the

01:09:50.310 --> 01:09:59.510
following statement be read into the record. Oh, let's read it.

01:10:00.090 --> 01:10:07.590
i have uh come to you from a planet in a different solar system i am an explorer in space stop right

01:10:07.590 --> 01:10:23.500
there let me see that forever this is a joke in very poor taste is it a joke to seek the truth

01:10:23.500 --> 01:10:30.000
about this man doctor's here you stayed here that a ship from outer space sank in an inland sea

01:10:30.000 --> 01:10:31.500
of our eastern desert.

01:10:31.600 --> 01:10:35.000
You also state the Bright Eyes had two intelligent companions

01:10:35.100 --> 01:10:37.170
with him at the time of his capture.

01:10:37.190 --> 01:10:39.190
That is his assertion.

01:10:39.190 --> 01:10:43.550
President, in addition to Bright Eyes,

01:10:43.650 --> 01:10:46.840
I believe the Prosecutor has reassembled

01:10:46.850 --> 01:10:50.370
all the surviving humans that were captured in the hunt.

01:10:50.390 --> 01:10:52.380
That's true, Dr. Sayes.

01:10:52.480 --> 01:10:53.400
Very well.

01:10:54.330 --> 01:10:55.890
I suggest it'll be.

01:10:56.260 --> 01:10:58.960
Go take a look at it.

01:11:36.460 --> 01:11:38.410
That's him, that's Lennon!

01:11:38.410 --> 01:11:39.560
Which one?

01:11:39.560 --> 01:11:43.810
The tall one, in the back.

01:11:43.810 --> 01:11:46.810
Do you acknowledge kinship with any of these creatures?

01:11:46.810 --> 01:11:47.810
With one of them, yes.

01:11:47.810 --> 01:11:52.780
Identify him then, speak to him!

01:11:52.780 --> 01:11:56.610
Lennon?

01:12:03.930 --> 01:12:08.580
Did you know about this?

01:12:08.580 --> 01:12:12.860
No, I swear I never saw this man before.

01:12:12.860 --> 01:12:21.520
But they cut up his brain, you bloody baboon!

01:12:21.520 --> 01:12:22.790
Stop it!

01:12:36.200 --> 01:12:36.720
Let's hide.

01:13:18.750 --> 01:13:20.670
Mr. President, a word of explanation.

01:13:21.920 --> 01:13:24.030
The human specimen you saw

01:13:24.030 --> 01:13:26.250
outside suffered a skull fracture

01:13:26.250 --> 01:13:27.470
in the court of the hunt.

01:13:28.160 --> 01:13:30.000
Two fine veterinary surgeons

01:13:30.250 --> 01:13:33.160
under my direction were able to save his life.

01:13:33.430 --> 01:13:36.510
But the beast could not speak, of course.

01:13:36.610 --> 01:13:38.210
Nor will he ever speak.

01:13:38.310 --> 01:13:40.100
You did that to him, damn you!

01:13:40.200 --> 01:13:42.600
You cut out his memory, you took his identity,

01:13:42.700 --> 01:13:44.100
and that's what you want to do to me!

01:13:44.200 --> 01:13:46.610
Pailiff, gag the animal!

01:13:46.880 --> 01:13:48.370
Damn you!

01:13:51.100 --> 01:13:52.990
May it please a triangle.

01:13:53.060 --> 01:13:54.860
I, for one, grant you that this creature

01:13:54.960 --> 01:13:56.560
cannot have come from another planet.

01:13:56.660 --> 01:13:58.220
But this much is certain.

01:13:58.470 --> 01:14:00.000
He does come from somewhere in the

01:14:00.000 --> 01:14:04.780
He's described the region to us, and described it accurately, for I have been there.

01:14:04.780 --> 01:14:06.600
You visited the Forbidden Zone?

01:14:06.600 --> 01:14:10.700
Yes, sir. A year ago, with the special permission of the Academy.

01:14:10.700 --> 01:14:15.580
He exceeded his orders. His travel permit was cancelled immediately.

01:14:15.580 --> 01:14:17.530
Yes, sir. That is true, thanks to you.

01:14:17.530 --> 01:14:25.620
But not before I discovered evidence of a simian culture that existed long before the sacred scrolls were written.

01:14:25.620 --> 01:14:29.670
Objection! These remarks are profane and irrelevant.

01:14:30.060 --> 01:14:35.340
Your archaeological theories have no bearing on the disposition of this creature.

01:14:35.550 --> 01:14:38.600
Let them talk, Mr. President. Let them talk.

01:14:39.030 --> 01:14:43.730
Sirs, our theories have a bearing on his identity.

01:14:43.760 --> 01:14:48.850
- How so? - Well, let us assume, as common sense dictates,

01:14:48.930 --> 01:14:51.440
that the prisoner's story is false.

01:14:51.760 --> 01:14:54.930
But if he did not come from another planet,

01:14:55.270 --> 01:14:58.610
then surely he sprang from our own.

01:15:02.720 --> 01:15:08.640
I have found no physiological defect to explain why humans are mute.

01:15:08.720 --> 01:15:10.540
Objection! Sustain!

01:15:10.620 --> 01:15:12.580
Their speech organs are adequate.

01:15:12.660 --> 01:15:15.730
The floor lies not in anatomy, but in the brain.

01:15:15.810 --> 01:15:17.570
Objection! Sustain!

01:15:17.650 --> 01:15:21.570
Sustain all objections, but face the truth.

01:15:21.640 --> 01:15:26.170
Yes. Behold this marvel, this living paradox,

01:15:26.250 --> 01:15:28.740
this missing link in an evolutionary chain.

01:15:28.820 --> 01:15:30.000
Silence it!

01:15:31.440 --> 01:15:34.440
I think an indictment is in order.

01:15:34.540 --> 01:15:37.490
Yes, sir. The state charges Dr. Zeera and Cornelius

01:15:37.590 --> 01:15:42.200
with contempt of this tribunal, malicious mischief and scientific heresy.

01:15:42.300 --> 01:15:46.530
It's so ordered. This tribunal will examine all the evidence presented here

01:15:46.630 --> 01:15:50.610
and in due course render its verdict as to the proposed indictment

01:15:50.710 --> 01:15:55.990
and as to the disposition of the deviant in question.

01:15:55.990 --> 01:15:58.770
This hearing is adjourned.

01:16:46.280 --> 01:16:47.060
I'm not sure.

01:17:00.000 --> 01:17:06.940
At the moment, your two simian friends and sponsors are free on bail.

01:17:07.040 --> 01:17:10.290
But they'll soon be brought to trial for heresy.

01:17:10.390 --> 01:17:15.580
- What about me? - Oh, your case was preordained.

01:17:15.680 --> 01:17:19.060
In a way, you did the state of service.

01:17:19.160 --> 01:17:23.870
Because you made it possible for us to expose Zera and Cornelius.

01:17:23.970 --> 01:17:30.000
Now the tribunal has placed you in my custody for final decision.

01:17:30.000 --> 01:17:41.160
position. Do you realize what that means? No. Emasculation to begin with, then experimental

01:17:41.160 --> 01:17:50.660
surgery on the speech centers, on the brain. Eventually a kind of living death. However,

01:17:53.680 --> 01:17:59.480
I have it in my power to grant a deprive. That is why I summoned you here tonight.

01:18:01.530 --> 01:18:05.630
Tell me who and what you really are and where you came from,

01:18:05.920 --> 01:18:07.940
and no veterinary shall touch you.

01:18:08.080 --> 01:18:10.740
I told you that at that hewing of yours.

01:18:10.820 --> 01:18:14.330
You lied! Where is your tribe?

01:18:15.230 --> 01:18:16.230
My tribe?

01:18:16.510 --> 01:18:20.330
They live on another planet in another solar system.

01:18:20.650 --> 01:18:23.530
Even in your lies, some truth slips through.

01:18:23.530 --> 01:18:28.370
That mythical community you're supposed to come from, Fort Wayne.

01:18:28.610 --> 01:18:29.330
What about it?

01:18:29.380 --> 01:18:29.880
A fort?

01:18:31.980 --> 01:18:35.490
- Unconsciously you chose a name that was belligerent.

01:18:35.490 --> 01:18:38.250
Where were you nurtured?

01:18:38.250 --> 01:18:42.270
- Then you don't believe that prosecutor's charge

01:18:42.270 --> 01:18:45.390
that I'm a monster created by Dr. Zira?

01:18:45.390 --> 01:18:48.410
- Certainly not.

01:18:48.410 --> 01:18:52.650
- Ah, you're a mutant.

01:18:52.650 --> 01:18:54.510
- That's what Zira and Cornelius claim.

01:18:54.510 --> 01:18:56.770
You're talking heresy, Doctor.

01:18:56.770 --> 01:18:59.220
- Of course, so suppose I am a mutant.

01:19:00.000 --> 01:19:03.560
How can the appearance of one mutant send you into a panic?

01:19:03.720 --> 01:19:06.880
Because you're not unique. There's a one you call Landon.

01:19:07.280 --> 01:19:09.010
You admit that...

01:19:09.010 --> 01:19:14.430
I admit that where there's one mutant, there's probably another and another and another, a whole nest of them.

01:19:16.070 --> 01:19:19.800
Where is your nest, Taylor? Where are your women?

01:19:20.260 --> 01:19:23.850
Thank you. Thank you for calling me Taylor.

01:19:24.830 --> 01:19:30.000
Dr. Zayas, I know who I am, but who are you?

01:19:31.370 --> 01:19:39.030
in hell did this upside-down civilization get started you may well call it upside down since

01:19:39.030 --> 01:19:50.010
you occupy its lowest level and deservedly so our eastern desert has never been explored because we've

01:19:50.010 --> 01:20:00.000
always assumed that life cannot exist there taylor save yourself tell me is there another jungle

01:20:00.030 --> 01:20:02.170
beyond the forbidden zone.

01:20:02.270 --> 01:20:03.310
I don't know.

01:20:04.380 --> 01:20:06.970
If you're trying to protect others of your kind,

01:20:07.540 --> 01:20:09.020
it'll cost you your identity.

01:20:09.360 --> 01:20:10.620
I'm not protecting anyone.

01:20:11.020 --> 01:20:12.980
This whole thing is insane.

01:20:13.320 --> 01:20:14.180
What have I done?

01:20:21.860 --> 01:20:24.710
Walking pestilence.

01:20:25.780 --> 01:20:27.600
I do know who you are, Taylor.

01:20:30.570 --> 01:20:34.130
I'll give you just six hours to make a full confession.

01:20:34.210 --> 01:20:37.230
After that, I shall use surgery to obtain one.

01:20:37.320 --> 01:20:40.570
- Darts! - All right, you can cut pieces out of me.

01:20:40.650 --> 01:20:44.250
- You've got the power. - Return this creature to his cage.

01:20:44.330 --> 01:20:47.290
What you do about it, Peter? Remember that! Remember that!

01:20:47.370 --> 01:20:50.640
Because you're afraid of me! What are you afraid of, Doctor?

01:21:13.600 --> 01:21:15.970
- Are you Julius? - Who are you?

01:21:16.050 --> 01:21:18.210
I'm from the Office of Animal Affairs.

01:21:20.960 --> 01:21:24.000
That mail is to be transferred to the zoo.

01:21:24.520 --> 01:21:27.440
At this hour? Who says so?

01:21:28.000 --> 01:21:29.600
Don't they tell you anything?

01:21:30.380 --> 01:21:34.180
The anti-vivisectionist society is up in arms.

01:21:34.180 --> 01:21:38.160
They're gonna save this beast from those butchers in the lab.

01:21:38.160 --> 01:21:41.620
If he can speak, he belongs in a public zoo.

01:21:41.620 --> 01:21:44.200
But what'll probably happen is that some money-mad grown-up

01:21:44.200 --> 01:21:46.640
will put him in a circus, and then we'll have to pay to see--

01:21:46.640 --> 01:21:50.070
Stop making speeches and show me the order.

01:22:06.680 --> 01:22:11.710
this order is no good it must be countersigned by Dr. Zaius

01:22:15.360 --> 01:22:26.950
can't talk i'm Dr. Zira's nephew this abduction was her idea

01:22:26.950 --> 01:22:30.000
you're not really going to the zoo that's just our story in case something

01:22:30.000 --> 01:22:31.000
Somebody stops us.

01:22:31.000 --> 01:22:34.620
Get me out of this.

01:22:34.620 --> 01:22:36.790
Gotta move fast.

01:22:36.790 --> 01:22:41.870
There's a lot too.

01:22:41.870 --> 01:22:43.950
Zira doesn't want your female.

01:22:43.950 --> 01:22:44.950
I want her.

01:22:44.950 --> 01:22:49.400
You insist, but I'm not taking any orders.

01:22:49.400 --> 01:22:50.580
All right, come on, let's go.

01:23:14.560 --> 01:23:30.000
told you not to bring the other one he wouldn't leave her right come on come on you're having

01:23:30.190 --> 01:23:33.190
What do you expect, an ape's new suit?

01:23:33.190 --> 01:23:35.330
Stuff stinks.

01:23:35.330 --> 01:23:37.330
Well, so do you, like all men.

01:23:37.330 --> 01:23:41.230
Taylor, remember, all men look alike to most apes.

01:23:41.230 --> 01:23:45.230
So put it on and keep quiet, and we may just get away with this.

01:23:45.230 --> 01:23:46.230
Hurry!

01:25:04.990 --> 01:25:06.930
Well, Taylor, we're all fugitives now.

01:25:07.550 --> 01:25:09.560
Do you have any weapons, any guns?

01:25:10.160 --> 01:25:12.050
The best, but we won't need them.

01:25:12.550 --> 01:25:14.750
I'm glad to hear it. I want one anyway.

01:25:24.210 --> 01:25:26.030
Now look here, Taylor, I'm in charge of this expedition.

01:25:26.370 --> 01:25:29.050
Good for you, but you're not in charge of me.

01:25:29.310 --> 01:25:29.800
Not anymore.

01:25:30.540 --> 01:25:35.700
- I don't plan to be caught again. - As you wish.

01:25:36.100 --> 01:25:39.960
Dr. Zayas seemed to think there was another jungle beyond the Forbidden Zone.

01:25:40.200 --> 01:25:43.130
- Try for that. - What about you?

01:25:43.360 --> 01:25:46.010
Cornelius and I have been indicted for heresy.

01:25:46.140 --> 01:25:49.560
Unless we can prove our theories, we don't stand a chance of acquittal.

01:25:49.820 --> 01:25:51.740
You're going back to the Forbidden Zone?

01:25:51.920 --> 01:25:54.960
We're going back to the diggings I worked out over a year ago.

01:25:55.180 --> 01:25:57.710
It's a three-day ride across the desert,

01:25:58.020 --> 01:26:00.000
near the place where you claim you landed from that point.

01:26:00.060 --> 01:26:04.930
planet of yours. You still don't believe me, do you? It's a long detour to Dead Lake. What would

01:26:04.930 --> 01:26:12.450
we find? Nothing much. An empty rubber life raft, maybe a little flag, the emblem of my countrymen.

01:26:13.470 --> 01:26:18.760
The terrain around that lake is poisonous. There's no fresh water, no vegetation, nothing.

01:26:24.830 --> 01:26:30.000
I ought to thank you for saving me. You'll be in trouble for that. We've been in

01:26:30.000 --> 01:26:32.200
In trouble since the moment we met you.

01:26:34.590 --> 01:26:37.790
What's she pointing at?

01:26:38.270 --> 01:26:39.810
This must be close to home for her.

01:26:39.890 --> 01:26:40.490
She knows it.

01:26:45.120 --> 01:26:50.490
It's not safe.

01:26:52.130 --> 01:26:56.480
Better get started.

01:26:56.820 --> 01:26:59.550
If the Mounted Police pick up our trail, they'll come this far at least.

01:26:59.750 --> 01:27:00.000
Right.

01:27:00.280 --> 01:27:02.530
Let's get the water and provisions into the wagon.

01:28:22.400 --> 01:28:29.120
to it flows into a sea some miles from here that's where we'll find the diggings beyond that

01:28:30.000 --> 01:28:36.530
I don't know. You can't ride along the shore at high tide, and we had no boats on our last expedition.

01:28:37.510 --> 01:28:40.670
You never told me. Why do you call this a forbidden zone?

01:28:41.780 --> 01:28:47.350
No one knows. It's an ancient taboo set forth in the sacred scrolls.

01:28:47.630 --> 01:28:50.150
The lawgiver pronounced this whole area deadly.

01:28:52.940 --> 01:28:54.380
Shouldn't we be moving on?

01:28:55.870 --> 01:28:56.630
Time for that.

01:30:33.610 --> 01:30:36.110
Why did you do that? Scrape off your hair.

01:30:36.230 --> 01:30:39.970
In my world, when I left it, only kids your age wore beards.

01:30:41.060 --> 01:30:44.010
Beards? I don't go in for fads.

01:30:45.530 --> 01:30:49.710
Somehow, it makes you look less intelligent.

01:30:51.570 --> 01:30:53.530
When will you show me what's in that cave?

01:30:54.110 --> 01:30:55.340
Right now, if you like.

01:31:35.500 --> 01:31:39.000
- If there's any more shooting, Dr. Zayas, you'll be the first to go.

01:31:39.000 --> 01:31:40.390
You can count on it!

01:31:40.390 --> 01:31:43.290
- Taylor, you are not in command here. Put down that gun!

01:31:43.290 --> 01:31:44.720
- Shut up!

01:31:44.720 --> 01:31:48.050
Very well. Lower your weapons.

01:31:48.050 --> 01:31:50.170
Tell him to pull back around the rocks.

01:31:50.170 --> 01:31:53.810
Out of range. Withdrawal!

01:32:00.540 --> 01:32:02.000
How did you know we'd come here?

01:32:02.000 --> 01:32:06.430
It wasn't difficult. Only an apostate would flee to the Forbidden Zone.

01:32:06.430 --> 01:32:10.660
And only a fool would give a gun to an animal.

01:32:10.660 --> 01:32:13.910
I see you've brought the female of your species.

01:32:13.910 --> 01:32:17.680
I didn't realize that man could be monogamous.

01:32:17.680 --> 01:32:21.630
On this planet, it's easy.

01:32:21.630 --> 01:32:25.290
I asked you to reconsider the rash course you've undertaken.

01:32:25.290 --> 01:32:30.000
If you're convicted of heresy, the most you'll get is two years.

01:32:30.190 --> 01:32:35.100
If you persist in pointing guns in my direction, you'll hang for high treason.

01:32:36.210 --> 01:32:37.890
We never meant to be treasonous, sir.

01:32:38.750 --> 01:32:42.090
But up there, in the face of that cliff, there is a vast cave.

01:32:42.660 --> 01:32:46.100
And in that cave, a fabulous treasure of fossils and artifacts.

01:32:46.650 --> 01:32:49.590
I've seen some of your fossils and artifacts.

01:32:49.890 --> 01:32:50.330
They're worth it.

01:32:50.330 --> 01:32:52.010
There's your Minister of Science.

01:32:52.370 --> 01:32:55.470
Honor-bound to expand the frontiers of knowledge.

01:32:55.650 --> 01:32:56.460
Taylor, please.

01:32:56.620 --> 01:32:58.840
Except that he's also Chief Defender of the Faith.

01:32:58.920 --> 01:33:00.000
There is no contest.

01:33:00.000 --> 01:33:03.940
a contradiction between faith and science, true science.

01:33:04.040 --> 01:33:06.140
Are you willing to put that statement to the test?

01:33:06.240 --> 01:33:08.140
- Taylor, I would much rather than-- - Take it easy.

01:33:08.240 --> 01:33:09.940
You saved me from this fanatic.

01:33:10.040 --> 01:33:12.130
Maybe I can return the favor.

01:33:12.500 --> 01:33:14.490
What is your proposal?

01:33:14.990 --> 01:33:17.800
When were those sacred scrolls of yours written?

01:33:17.930 --> 01:33:19.840
Twelve hundred years ago.

01:33:19.960 --> 01:33:21.030
All right.

01:33:21.230 --> 01:33:22.630
Now, if they can prove those scrolls,

01:33:22.730 --> 01:33:24.430
don't tell the whole truth of your history.

01:33:24.530 --> 01:33:27.880
If they can find some real evidence of another culture

01:33:27.980 --> 01:33:29.860
from some remote past.

01:33:30.030 --> 01:33:31.730
- Will you let them off?

01:33:31.730 --> 01:33:32.910
- Of course.

01:33:32.910 --> 01:33:39.840
- Let's go up to the cave.

01:33:39.840 --> 01:33:41.700
- Sorry, Lucius, you've got to stay here

01:33:41.700 --> 01:33:42.780
and guard the camp.

01:33:42.780 --> 01:33:46.060
- Always giving orders, just like every other adult.

01:33:46.060 --> 01:33:48.600
- Relax, you'll get to see it all later on.

01:34:51.340 --> 01:34:52.940
Present your evidence, Cornelius.

01:34:53.660 --> 01:35:00.000
It was at this level that I discovered traces of an early ape creature, a stage of primitive

01:35:00.000 --> 01:35:07.960
barbarism really dating back some 1300 years roughly it was at this level i discovered cutting

01:35:07.960 --> 01:35:15.720
tools and arrowheads of quartz and the fossilized bones of carnivorous gorillas but the artifacts

01:35:15.720 --> 01:35:30.000
lying here were found at this level and date back as 700 years earlier that's the paradox for the more ancient

01:35:30.000 --> 01:35:31.700
is the more advanced.

01:35:31.800 --> 01:35:35.490
Now, admittedly, many of these objects are unidentified,

01:35:35.590 --> 01:35:37.490
but clearly they were fashioned by beings

01:35:37.590 --> 01:35:39.690
with a knowledge of metallurgy.

01:35:39.790 --> 01:35:44.270
Indeed, the fact that many of these tools are unknown to us

01:35:44.370 --> 01:35:48.970
suggests a culture which, in certain ways, equals our own.

01:35:49.070 --> 01:35:51.650
Some of the evidence is uncontestable.

01:35:51.750 --> 01:35:55.650
Don't speak to me in absolutes. The evidence is contestable.

01:35:55.750 --> 01:35:58.280
I apologize, sir.

01:35:58.380 --> 01:36:00.000
Begin with your metallurgy.

01:36:00.030 --> 01:36:03.080
of dating the past accrued to say the least.

01:36:03.150 --> 01:36:07.270
There are geologists from my staff who would laugh at your speculations.

01:36:07.280 --> 01:36:10.020
- But there's the doll, sir. - What?

01:36:10.540 --> 01:36:14.630
Oh, lying right there, the human doll.

01:36:19.120 --> 01:36:25.160
What does this prove? My granddaughter plays with human dolls.

01:36:26.070 --> 01:36:29.670
The doll was found beside the jawbone of a man.

01:36:30.000 --> 01:36:33.600
and no trace of simian fossil has been found in this deposit.

01:36:33.600 --> 01:36:35.760
Your conclusion is premature.

01:36:35.760 --> 01:36:39.600
Have you forgotten your scripture, the 13th scroll?

01:36:39.600 --> 01:36:42.600
And Proteus brought the upright beast into the garden

01:36:42.600 --> 01:36:46.400
and chained him to a tree, and the children did make sport of him.

01:36:46.400 --> 01:36:48.280
No, sir, I have not forgotten.

01:36:48.280 --> 01:36:53.190
Well, for a time, the ancients kept humans as household pets

01:36:53.190 --> 01:36:58.240
until our lawgiver proved that man could not be tamed.

01:36:58.240 --> 01:37:00.000
Keep digging, Cornelius.

01:37:00.000 --> 01:37:12.210
find evidence of the master of this house. An ape. What are you doing? Reconstructing

01:37:12.210 --> 01:37:20.930
a past life. You say these things were found at the same level as that dog? Whoever owned

01:37:20.930 --> 01:37:30.000
him must have been in pretty bad shape. He wore false teeth and eyeglasses. He had a

01:37:32.140 --> 01:37:38.800
Towards the end he had this prefabricated valve put in it.

01:37:38.800 --> 01:37:41.770
- I don't say he was a man like I knew at home,

01:37:41.770 --> 01:37:43.970
but he must have been a close relative

01:37:43.970 --> 01:37:46.360
because he had all the same weaknesses.

01:37:46.360 --> 01:37:53.290
He was a weak, fragile animal, but he was here before you,

01:37:53.290 --> 01:37:55.140
and he was better than you are.

01:37:55.140 --> 01:37:57.230
- That's lunacy.

01:37:57.230 --> 01:38:00.000
I can offer alternate descriptions of every one of those.

01:38:00.000 --> 01:38:03.000
which is just as ingenious as yours,

01:38:03.000 --> 01:38:06.200
but it'd be conjecture, not proof.

01:38:06.200 --> 01:38:23.670
Zaius would an ape make a human doll.

01:38:30.990 --> 01:38:37.400
- Dirty! - Get over!

01:39:37.450 --> 01:39:55.700
Kill you right now.

01:40:06.200 --> 01:40:27.650
Lucius, are you all right?

01:40:27.650 --> 01:40:30.000
They took me by surprise.

01:40:30.000 --> 01:40:39.530
surprise sneaked up on me while i was feeding the horses what's happened to honor i got off two

01:40:39.530 --> 01:40:46.890
rounds to warn you they've taken everything not quite everything they left a hostage behind

01:40:46.890 --> 01:40:54.050
how are you feeling disillusioned you can't trust the older generation i know what you mean

01:40:54.050 --> 01:40:59.540
i want you to go around the rocks and tell those gorillas i've got dr zayas prisoner

01:41:00.440 --> 01:41:01.580
Yes, I can do that.

01:41:01.920 --> 01:41:03.580
I want a horse, food and water.

01:41:03.780 --> 01:41:06.020
Enough for a week for me and this female.

01:41:06.410 --> 01:41:08.060
And 50 rounds of ammunition.

01:41:08.640 --> 01:41:10.590
What if they won't agree to your terms?

01:41:10.810 --> 01:41:12.010
Tell them I'll shoot him.

01:41:12.670 --> 01:41:14.150
Taylor, you can't.

01:41:14.630 --> 01:41:16.090
Ah, yes, he can.

01:41:17.580 --> 01:41:19.130
He's a born killer.

01:41:19.890 --> 01:41:20.950
Deliver the message.

01:41:23.790 --> 01:41:24.390
Over here.

01:41:30.000 --> 01:42:00.000
like that why not it's humiliating the way I was humiliated by all of you let me

01:42:00.000 --> 01:42:01.180
around on a leash.

01:42:01.340 --> 01:42:02.020
That was different.

01:42:02.340 --> 01:42:03.440
We thought you were inferior.

01:42:04.170 --> 01:42:05.070
Now you know better.

01:42:06.790 --> 01:42:08.010
Cornelius was right, Doctor.

01:42:08.400 --> 01:42:09.300
He proved it.

01:42:10.080 --> 01:42:11.280
Man was here first.

01:42:11.440 --> 01:42:13.360
You owe him your science, your culture,

01:42:13.920 --> 01:42:15.520
whatever civilization you've got.

01:42:15.640 --> 01:42:16.700
Then answer be this.

01:42:17.220 --> 01:42:18.780
If man was superior,

01:42:19.450 --> 01:42:20.530
why didn't he survive?

01:42:21.220 --> 01:42:22.390
Wiped out by a plague,

01:42:22.490 --> 01:42:23.910
some natural catastrophe.

01:42:24.790 --> 01:42:25.950
Storm of meteors.

01:42:26.050 --> 01:42:27.370
In the looks of some parts of this planet,

01:42:27.470 --> 01:42:28.630
I'd say that was a fair bet.

01:42:28.880 --> 01:42:30.000
But we can't be sure.

01:42:31.180 --> 01:42:35.760
He is. He knew all the time, long before you found your cave.

01:42:35.940 --> 01:42:38.760
He knew. Defender of the faith.

01:42:38.960 --> 01:42:42.000
Guardian of the terrible secret. That's it, isn't it, Doctor?

01:42:42.280 --> 01:42:45.220
What I know of man was written long ago.

01:42:45.480 --> 01:42:48.720
Set down by the greatest ape of all, our lawgiver.

01:42:49.740 --> 01:42:53.760
Cornelius, come here. Reach into my pocket.

01:42:54.810 --> 01:42:58.730
Read to him the 29th scroll. Sixth verse.

01:43:03.000 --> 01:43:09.530
Beware the beast man for he is the devil's pawn. Alone among God's primates

01:43:09.790 --> 01:43:18.650
He kills for sport or lust or greed. Yea, he will murder his brother to possess his brother's land.

01:43:18.970 --> 01:43:24.810
Let him not breed in great numbers for he will make a desert of his home and

01:43:25.370 --> 01:43:30.000
yours. Shun him, drive him back into his

01:43:30.000 --> 01:43:38.610
his jungle there for he is the harbinger of death I found nothing in the cave to

01:43:38.610 --> 01:43:53.400
alter that conception of man and I still live by its injunction far enough

01:44:00.670 --> 01:44:02.570
They think you're behaving foolishly.

01:44:04.220 --> 01:44:05.580
I must say I agree.

01:44:06.420 --> 01:44:07.300
Where will you go?

01:44:08.160 --> 01:44:11.220
To start with, I'll follow the shoreline in my nose.

01:44:11.880 --> 01:44:14.840
Suppose you find nothing but a wasteland.

01:44:15.630 --> 01:44:16.450
How will you survive?

01:44:17.180 --> 01:44:18.560
He won't survive.

01:44:28.850 --> 01:44:29.940
How about coming along?

01:44:30.730 --> 01:44:31.570
We can't.

01:44:31.940 --> 01:44:34.130
It's better than going to jail for heresy.

01:44:34.460 --> 01:44:35.980
Oh, they can't convict us of heresy.

01:44:36.590 --> 01:44:37.830
You've helped prove our innocence.

01:44:38.740 --> 01:44:42.740
Besides, his culture is our culture.

01:44:44.200 --> 01:44:46.410
Well, good luck then.

01:44:53.020 --> 01:44:53.420
Lucius?

01:44:54.440 --> 01:44:57.130
I still say you're making a mistake.

01:44:57.730 --> 01:44:59.390
That's the spirit. Keep him flying.

01:45:00.060 --> 01:45:02.900
- What? - The flags of discontent.

01:45:02.900 --> 01:45:05.120
Remember, never trust anybody over 30.

01:45:05.120 --> 01:45:08.870
Doctor, I'd like to kiss you goodbye.

01:45:08.870 --> 01:45:20.710
All right. You're so damned ugly.

01:45:46.730 --> 01:45:50.140
- Don't try to follow us, I'm pretty handy with this.

01:45:50.140 --> 01:45:52.140
- Of that I'm sure.

01:45:52.140 --> 01:45:56.490
All my life I've awaited your coming and dreaded it.

01:45:56.490 --> 01:45:57.870
Like death itself.

01:45:57.870 --> 01:45:59.170
- Why?

01:45:59.170 --> 01:46:00.000
- I've terrified you.

01:46:00.000 --> 01:46:02.300
- Are you from the first doctor? - I still do.

01:46:02.300 --> 01:46:04.770
You're afraid of me and you hate me.

01:46:04.770 --> 01:46:07.390
- Why? - Because you're a man.

01:46:07.390 --> 01:46:13.660
And you're right. I have always known about man.

01:46:13.660 --> 01:46:19.560
From the evidence, I believe his wisdom must walk hand in hand with his idiocy.

01:46:19.560 --> 01:46:22.500
His emotions must rule his brain.

01:46:22.500 --> 01:46:28.680
He must be a warlike creature who gives battle to everything around you, even himself.

01:46:28.680 --> 01:46:29.640
What evidence?

01:46:30.060 --> 01:46:31.620
There were no weapons in that cave.

01:46:32.080 --> 01:46:34.460
The Forbidden Zone was once a paradise.

01:46:35.520 --> 01:46:39.480
Your breed made a desert of it, ages ago.

01:46:39.860 --> 01:46:41.340
It still doesn't give me the why.

01:46:42.010 --> 01:46:47.310
A planet where apes evolved from men, there's got to be an answer.

01:46:48.160 --> 01:46:49.660
Don't look for it, Taylor.

01:46:50.570 --> 01:46:53.290
You may not like what you find.

01:47:02.170 --> 01:47:03.130
Untie me.

01:47:04.000 --> 01:47:30.000
You're going to seal up the case.

01:47:31.880 --> 01:47:32.780
Seal the cave.

01:47:32.780 --> 01:47:35.980
That is correct, and you will both stand trial for heresy.

01:47:36.370 --> 01:47:38.070
But the proof! The doll!

01:47:38.070 --> 01:47:40.470
In a few minutes, there will be no doll.

01:47:40.980 --> 01:47:42.890
The card game. I'm sorry.

01:47:43.750 --> 01:47:46.550
Dr. Zaius! Dr. Zaius, you mustn't! You promised!

01:47:46.550 --> 01:47:49.550
What I do, I do with no pleasure. Silence!

01:47:49.550 --> 01:47:50.250
Doctor?

01:47:51.050 --> 01:47:54.460
Dr. Zaius, this is inexcusable!

01:47:54.740 --> 01:47:57.120
Why must knowledge stand still?

01:47:57.660 --> 01:47:59.220
What about the future?

01:48:00.890 --> 01:48:02.920
I may just have saved it for you.

01:48:05.190 --> 01:48:08.390
What will he find out there, Doctor?

01:48:09.120 --> 01:48:11.240
His destiny.

01:49:00.000 --> 01:49:00.420
We'll see you next time.
